Do not edit the generated index by hand.\u003C/p>\n",{"headings":44,"localImagePaths":45,"remoteImagePaths":46,"frontmatter":47,"imagePaths":48},[],[],[],{"title":32,"description":33},[],"reference",{"id":49,"data":51,"body":57,"filePath":58,"digest":59,"rendered":60},{"title":52,"description":53,"editUrl":14,"head":54,"template":35,"sidebar":55,"pagefind":14,"draft":7},"Commands and model","Command reference and the ADR record shape.",[],{"hidden":7,"attrs":56},{},"| Command | Purpose |\n| --- | --- |\n| `adr init` | Create the ADR directory, template, and empty index |\n| `adr new \"Title\"` | Create a numbered ADR |\n| `adr list` | List records with status, tag, and scope filters |\n| `adr show \u003Cid>` | Show one ADR’s metadata and governance fields |\n| `adr check adr` | Validate ADR files |\n| `adr index` | Generate or check the YAML index |\n| `adr bs-detector --base \u003Cref>` | Find ADRs applicable to changed Git paths |\n\nEach record combines YAML frontmatter with `Context`, `Decision`, `Alternatives Considered`, and `Consequences` sections. Use constraints for implementation rules and invariants for properties that must remain true.\n\nJSON is available for automation:\n\n```bash\nadr list --format json\nadr show --format json ADR-0001\n```","src/content/docs/reference.md","5bdb901bfc7ae154",{"html":61,"metadata":62},"\u003Ctable>\n\u003Cthead>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Cth>Command\u003C/th>\n\u003Cth>Purpose\u003C/th>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003C/thead>\n\u003Ctbody>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">adr init\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Create the ADR directory, template, and empty index\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">adr new \"Title\"\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Create a numbered ADR\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">adr list\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>List records with status, tag, and scope filters\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">adr show &lt;id&gt;\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Show one ADR’s metadata and governance fields\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">adr check adr\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Validate ADR files\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">adr index\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Generate or check the YAML index\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003Ctr>\n\u003Ctd>\u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">adr bs-detector --base &lt;ref&gt;\u003C/code>\u003C/td>\n\u003Ctd>Find ADRs applicable to changed Git paths\u003C/td>\n\u003C/tr>\n\u003C/tbody>\n\u003C/table>\n\u003Cp>Each record combines YAML frontmatter with \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">Context\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">Decision\u003C/code>, \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">Alternatives Considered\u003C/code>, and \u003Ccode dir=\"auto\">Consequences\u003C/code> sections. Use constraints for implementation rules and invariants for properties that must remain true.\u003C/p>\n\u003Cp>JSON is available for automation:\u003C/p>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"expressive-code\">\u003Clink rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/adr-repo-governance/_astro/ec.w36nc.css\">\u003Cscript type=\"module\" src=\"/adr-repo-governance/_astro/ec.0vx5m.js\">\u003C/script>\u003Cfigure class=\"frame is-terminal not-content\">\u003Cfigcaption class=\"header\">\u003Cspan class=\"title\">\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"sr-only\">Terminal window\u003C/span>\u003C/figcaption>\u003Cpre data-language=\"bash\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cdiv class=\"ec-line\">\u003Cdiv class=\"code\">\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#82AAFF;--1:#3B61B0\">adr\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#D6DEEB;--1:#403F53\"> \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#ECC48D;--1:#3B61B0\">list\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#D6DEEB;--1:#403F53\"> \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#82AAFF;--1:#3B61B0\">--format\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#D6DEEB;--1:#403F53\"> \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#ECC48D;--1:#3B61B0\">json\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"ec-line\">\u003Cdiv class=\"code\">\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#82AAFF;--1:#3B61B0\">adr\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#D6DEEB;--1:#403F53\"> \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#ECC48D;--1:#3B61B0\">show\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#D6DEEB;--1:#403F53\"> \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#82AAFF;--1:#3B61B0\">--format\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#D6DEEB;--1:#403F53\"> \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#ECC48D;--1:#3B61B0\">json\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#D6DEEB;--1:#403F53\"> \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#ECC48D;--1:#3B61B0\">ADR-0001\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>\u003C/code>\u003C/pre>\u003Cdiv class=\"copy\">\u003Cdiv aria-live=\"polite\">\u003C/div>\u003Cbutton title=\"Copy to clipboard\" data-copied=\"Copied!\" data-code=\"adr list --format jsonadr show --format json ADR-0001\">\u003Cdiv>\u003C/div>\u003C/button>\u003C/div>\u003C/figure>\u003C/div>\n",{"headings":63,"localImagePaths":64,"remoteImagePaths":65,"frontmatter":66,"imagePaths":67},[],[],[],{"title":52,"description":53},[],"workflow",{"id":68,"data":70,"body":76,"filePath":77,"digest":78,"rendered":79},{"title":71,"description":72,"editUrl":14,"head":73,"template":35,"sidebar":74,"pagefind":14,"draft":7},"Workflow","The day-to-day workflow for creating and validating ADRs.",[],{"hidden":7,"attrs":75},{},"## Create a decision\n\n```bash\nadr init\nadr new --tags database,storage --paths \"src/db/**,migrations/**\" \"Use PostgreSQL for persistence\"\n```\n\nADRs live in `docs/adr/` by default. Scope paths tell reviewers which decisions may matter for a code change.\n\n## Review applicable decisions\n\n```bash\nadr bs-detector --base main\nadr list --path \"src/db/users.go\"\nadr show ADR-0001\n```\n\nThe detector is a review queue based on scope globs, not a semantic proof that the implementation complies.\n\n## Validate and index\n\n```bash\nadr check adr --strict\nadr index --check\n```\n\nThe index is generated metadata. Keep ADR Markdown as the source of truth and check the generated index in CI.","src/content/docs/workflow.md","55c7595a60757a90",{"html":80,"metadata":81},"\u003Cdiv class=\"sl-heading-wrapper level-h2\">\u003Ch2 id=\"create-a-decision\">Create a decision\u003C/h2>\u003Ca class=\"sl-anchor-link\" href=\"#create-a-decision\">\u003Cspan aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"sl-anchor-icon\">\u003Csvg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"currentColor\">\u003Cpath d=\"m12.11 15.39-3.88 3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1-3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0-3.5l3.88-3.88a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42l-3.88 3.89a4.48 4.48 0 0 0 6.33 6.33l3.89-3.88a1 1 0 0 0-1.42-1.42m8.58-12.08a4.49 4.49 0 0 0-6.33 0l-3.89 3.88a1 1 0 1 0 1.42 1.42l3.88-3.88a2.52 2.52 0 0 1 3.5 0 2.47 2.47 0 0 1 0 3.5l-3.88 3.88a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42 1 1 0 0 0 1.42 0l3.88-3.89a4.49 4.49 0 0 0 0-6.33M8.83 15.17a1 1 0 0 0 .71.29 1 1 0 0 0 .71-.29l4.92-4.92a1 1 0 1 0-1.42-1.42l-4.92 4.92a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.42\">\u003C/path>\u003C/svg>\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"sr-only\" data-pagefind-ignore>Section titled “Create a decision”\u003C/span>\u003C/a>\u003C/div>\n\u003Cdiv class=\"expressive-code\">\u003Clink rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/adr-repo-governance/_astro/ec.w36nc.css\">\u003Cscript type=\"module\" src=\"/adr-repo-governance/_astro/ec.0vx5m.js\">\u003C/script>\u003Cfigure class=\"frame is-terminal not-content\">\u003Cfigcaption class=\"header\">\u003Cspan class=\"title\">\u003C/span>\u003Cspan class=\"sr-only\">Terminal window\u003C/span>\u003C/figcaption>\u003Cpre data-language=\"bash\">\u003Ccode>\u003Cdiv class=\"ec-line\">\u003Cdiv class=\"code\">\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#82AAFF;--1:#3B61B0\">adr\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#D6DEEB;--1:#403F53\"> \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#ECC48D;--1:#3B61B0\">init\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"ec-line\">\u003Cdiv class=\"code\">\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#82AAFF;--1:#3B61B0\">adr\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#D6DEEB;--1:#403F53\"> \u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#ECC48D;--1:#3B61B0\">new\u003C/span>\u003Cspan style=\"--0:#D6DEEB;--1: